<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>netstandard2.1</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>True</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild Condition=" $(Configuration) == 'Release' ">true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile Condition=" $(Configuration) == 'Release' ">True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageId>FFmpegDotNet.Skia</PackageId>
		<Title>FFmpeg.Skia</Title>
		<Authors>Pascal Krenckel</Authors>
		<Description>
			Provides SkiaSharp integration for the FFmpeg .NET wrapper (FFmpegDotNet).
			Converts FFmpeg AVFrames to SKImage or SKBitmap and back, with crop, color space (YUV matrix, range, HDR) and alpha handling, and includes high-level classes (FFCodec2Skia, SKVideo, SKAnimatedImage) for decoding and rendering videos and animated images with Skia.
			The package version starts with the FFmpeg major version: 8.x for FFmpegDotNet 8 (FFmpeg 8.1), 9.x for FFmpegDotNet 9 (FFmpeg 9.0).
		</Description>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 Pascal Krenckel. All rights reserved.</Copyright>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Pascal-Krenckel/FFmpeg.Skia</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Pascal-Krenckel/FFmpeg.Skia</RepositoryUrl>
		<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
		<IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>ffmpeg; skia</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<!-- The version of FFmpeg.Skia itself; release tags are v$(SkiaVersion) (see .github/workflows/Release.yml) -->
		<SkiaVersion>3.0.0</SkiaVersion>
		<!-- FFmpegMajor.Major.Minor.Patch, like FFmpegDotNet: 8.3.0.0 is built for FFmpeg 8, 9.3.0.0 for FFmpeg 9 -->
		<Version>$(FFmpegMajor).$(SkiaVersion)</Version>
		<DefineConstants Condition="'$(FFmpegMajor)' == '9'">$(DefineConstants);FFMPEG9</DefineConstants>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			=== 3.0.0 ===
			Builds for FFmpeg 8 (FFmpegDotNet 8.x, package 8.3.0.0) and FFmpeg 9 (FFmpegDotNet 9.x, package 9.3.0.0) from the same sources. Use the package matching your FFmpegDotNet version.

			Breaking changes:
			- FFCodec2Skia.NextImage throws on decoding errors; false only means the end of the video.
			- FFCodec2Skia.Seek(TimeSpan) returns the frame visible at the requested time (was: the key frame before it); Seek(long) converts the frame number with the frame rate (FFmpeg's frame seeking is ignored by most formats).
			- Videos with non-square pixels are decoded with square pixels by default (FFCodec2Skia, SKVideo, SKAnimatedImage), e.g. 720x480 with 32:27 as 853x480.
			- AsSKBitmap, AsSKImage and FFCodec2Skia.Info use straight (Unpremul) alpha like FFmpeg; premultiplied Skia images are converted when copied into frames.
			- Bitmaps allocated for frames (CopyTo into an empty bitmap, SKAnimatedImage) use 8 bit color types; 10 bit video got RgbaF16.
			- YUV frames written from Skia without matrix or range are tagged BT.601 / limited range.
			- SKAnimatedImage.Start throws until the task returned by Stop has completed (two loops could run at the same time).
			- FFCodec2Skia.Create and SKAnimatedImage.Create throw for media without a video stream (ArgumentException / ArgumentOutOfRangeException) and dispose the media source.

			Bug fixes:
			- Copying frames with padded rows (most decoded frames) threw ArgumentOutOfRangeException (ToSKBitmap, ToSKImage, CopyTo, FFCodec2Skia, SKAnimatedImage).
			- SKImage/SKBitmap.ToAVFrame and CopyTo ignored the row bytes of the image: skewed images, and a heap overflow for images with padded rows (e.g. from AsSKImage).
			- FFCodec2Skia reused a scaler for bitmaps of another size: heap overflow.
			- Cropped frames: AsSKBitmap/AsSKImage/Reference used a wrong row offset; CopyTo and FFCodec2Skia ignored the crop.
			- SKBitmap.Reference wrote into the buffer of the previously referenced frame.
			- The YUV matrix (BT.709, BT.2020) and full range of yuv420p frames were ignored with FFmpeg 8 (converted as BT.601 limited range), in both directions.
			- HDR (PQ, HLG) was not tone mapped and wide gamuts were not mapped for Skia.
			- Frames marked interlaced lost every other line.
			- SKImage.ToAVFrame threw NullReferenceException for lazily decoded images; ToSKImage leaked an image.
			- FFCodec2Skia leaked the media source when creation failed; Duration was wrong for streams without duration.
			- SKVideo: Dispose after Stop threw; Dispose freed frames still used by the decoding thread or a handler; Restart while playing was not synchronized and lost the timing; seeking in Ended did not continue playback.
			- SKAnimatedImage: frames were shown for the duration of the next frame; Dispose during an operation could be undone; the AVFrame (and in DisposeAsync a bitmap) leaked; looping a still image busy-looped.

			New:
			- Rotation (display matrix, e.g. phone videos), SampleAspectRatio and DisplaySize on FFCodec2Skia, SKVideo and SKAnimatedImage; AVStream/AVFrame.GetDisplayRotation, AVStream.GetSampleAspectRatio; SKCanvas.DrawRotated.
			- SKVideo.Faulted event.
			- Colors are converted with FFmpeg's dynamic scaler with both FFmpeg versions, honoring YUV matrix, range and HDR metadata.

			Improvements:
			- The extension methods reuse their conversion setup (converting HDR frames took seconds per call).
			- SKAnimatedImage uses three buffers: Frame can be drawn from a render loop.
			- SKVideo and SKAnimatedImage may be disposed from any thread, including their event handlers.
			=== 2.3.0 ===
			Added SKAnimatedImage - a class that allows for both automatic and manual decoding auf image/video data.
			=== 2.2.0 ===
			AVFrame.CopyTo(SKBitmap) allows now empty bitmaps.
			SKBitmap.Reference(AVFrame). Same as AVFrame.AsSKBitmap(), just with an existing SKBitmap.
			=== 2.1.0 ===
			Added CopyTo-Extension that copies the content of SKBitmap/SKImage into an existing AVFrame
			BugFix: Removed blocking scheduler from SKVideo
			=== 2.0.0 ===
			Some smaller BugFixes
			Added xml docu into the package.
			Some functions got renamed.
	    </PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Condition="'$(FFmpegMajor)' == '8'" Include="FFmpegDotNet" Version="[8.1.2.15,9)" />
		<PackageReference Condition="'$(FFmpegMajor)' == '9'" Include="FFmpegDotNet" Version="[9.9.4,10)" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="10.0.400">
		  <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
		  <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
		</PackageReference>
		<PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" Version="4.151.1" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<Using Include="SkiaSharp" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<Target Name="CheckFFmpegMajor" BeforeTargets="Restore;CollectPackageReferences;Build">
		<Error Condition="'$(FFmpegMajor)' != '8' And '$(FFmpegMajor)' != '9'" Text="FFmpegMajor must be 8 or 9 (is '$(FFmpegMajor)')." />
	</Target>

</Project>
